.TH ESDM\-TOOL 1 "2026-08-05" "ESDM @VERSION@" "ESDM Manual"
.SH NAME
esdm\-tool \- query and control a running ESDM server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esdm\-tool
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esdm\-tool
is the command line client of
.BR esdm\-server (8).
It talks to the daemon over the RPC interface and covers three areas: querying
the status of the ESDM and its entropy sources, obtaining random data, and
administrative or diagnostic operations.
.PP
Options that change the state of the daemon go through the privileged RPC
interface and therefore require root; they are marked as such below. All other
operations work for any user that may access the unprivileged RPC socket.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increase logging verbosity. May be given repeatedly.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-decrease\-verbosity
Decrease logging verbosity. May be given repeatedly.
.TP
.B \-\-use\-syslog
Log to syslog instead of standard output and standard error.
.SS Status
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-status
Print the status of the ESDM and all of its entropy sources.
.TP
.B \-\-status\-json
Print the same information as a JSON document.
.TP
.BR \-J ", " \-\-jent\-status
Print the internal status of the Jitter RNG entropy source.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-is\-fully\-seeded
Exit successfully if the ESDM is fully seeded, i.e. ready to hand out random
data.
.TP
.B \-\-is\-running
Exit successfully if an
.BR esdm\-server (8)
is reachable.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-entropy\-count
Print the number of entropy bits accounted for in the auxiliary pool.
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-entropy\-level
Print the number of entropy bits accounted for in the internal state.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wait\-until\-seeded " \fITRIES\fR"
Poll the seeding state once per second, at most
.I TRIES
times, and exit as soon as the ESDM is fully seeded. Useful in service units
that must not start before random data of full quality is available.
.SS Obtaining random data
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-get\-random " \fIBYTES\fR"
Print
.I BYTES
random bytes, hex encoded by default.
.TP
.B \-\-get\-seed
Perform a get\-seed operation, i.e. obtain seed material together with its
entropy accounting.
.TP
.B \-\-raw\-bytes
Write the random data unencoded instead of hex encoded. Applies to
.B \-\-get\-random
and
.BR \-\-get\-seed .
.TP
.B \-\-use\-pr
Request the data from the prediction\-resistance generator, which reseeds from
the entropy sources for every request.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout\-msec " \fIMSEC\fR"
Bound
.B \-\-get\-random
by a timeout of
.I MSEC
milliseconds instead of blocking indefinitely.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-unseeded
Let
.B \-\-get\-random
and
.B \-\-get\-seed
proceed even though the ESDM is not fully seeded yet. The data is then not of
full quality.
.SS Administration
.TP
.BR \-W ", " \-\-write\-to\-aux\-pool " \fIDATA\fR"
Write the string
.I DATA
into the auxiliary pool. The argument is the data itself, not a byte count.
Requires root.
.TP
.BR \-B ", " \-\-write\-entropy\-bits " \fIBITS\fR"
Number of entropy bits the preceding write to the auxiliary pool is credited
with.
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-pool
Clear the entropy pool. Intended for testing. Requires root.
.TP
.B \-\-reseed\-crng
Force a reseed of the DRNGs. Intended for testing. Requires root.
.TP
.BR \-\-pkcs11\-pin " \fIPIN\fR"
Set the user PIN of the PKCS#11 entropy source. Pass
.B \-
to read the PIN from standard input with terminal echo disabled, which keeps
it out of the process table. May be combined with
.BR \-\-pkcs11\-token\-label .
Requires root.
.TP
.BR \-\-pkcs11\-token\-label " \fILABEL\fR"
Set the token label of the PKCS#11 entropy source and re\-open the module. Pass
an empty string to clear the override. Requires root.
.SS Benchmarking and stress testing
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-benchmark
Run a small speed test in full and prediction\-resistance mode across several
buffer sizes.
.TP
.BR \-\-benchmark\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Restrict the benchmark to one request mode:
.BR full ", " pr " or " both
(default:
.BR both ).
Implies
.BR \-\-benchmark .
.TP
.B \-\-stress\-delay
Run a single\-threaded delay measurement.
.TP
.B \-\-stress\-process
Run the delay stress test on all cores, using processes.
.TP
.B \-\-stress\-thread
Run the delay stress test on all cores, using threads.
.TP
.BR \-\-stress\-duration " \fISECS\fR"
Timeout of the stress tests. Default: 65.0.
.TP
.BR \-\-stress\-request\-size " \fIBYTES\fR"
Buffer size used by the stress tests. Default: 4.
.TP
.B \-\-stress\-cpu\-usage
Show CPU usage during the stress test.
.TP
.B \-\-stress\-fork
Check the fork handling of the RPC client library on the current platform.
.TP
.B \-\-stress\-init\-fini
Stress the init/fini reference counting of the RPC client library from several
threads.
.TP
.B \-\-endless\-stress
Run an endless stress test. Together with
.B \-\-continue\-on\-failure
the
.BR esdm\-server (8)
may be stopped and started while it runs.
.TP
.B \-\-continue\-on\-failure
Do not abort the test on the first failure.
.SS Testing helpers
The following options exist to study the behaviour of the auxiliary pool. They
seed the ESDM from the operating system RNG, which defeats the entropy
accounting of the ESDM.
.B Do not use them in production.
All of them require root.
.TP
.B \-\-seed\-via\-os
Single\-shot seeding of the auxiliary pool via
.BR getentropy (3)/ getrandom (2).
.TP
.B \-\-reseed\-via\-os
Automatic reseeding of the auxiliary pool from the same source.
.TP
.BR \-\-reseed\-delay\-ms " \fIMSEC\fR"
Delay inserted before each reseed, to emulate the latency of a smartcard or a
TPM.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B esdm\-tool
exits with status 0 on success. The query options
.RB ( \-\-is\-fully\-seeded ,
.BR \-\-is\-running ,
.BR \-\-wait\-until\-seeded )
report their answer through the exit status and are meant to be used in
scripts and service units.
.SH EXAMPLES
Wait up to a minute for the ESDM to become fully seeded, then draw 32 raw
random bytes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
esdm\-tool \-\-wait\-until\-seeded 60
esdm\-tool \-\-get\-random 32 \-\-raw\-bytes > seed.bin
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show the entropy source status as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
esdm\-tool \-\-status\-json
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esdm\-server (8),
.BR esdm\-kernel\-seeder (8),
.BR libesdm_rpc_client (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Stephan Mueller <smueller@chronox.de>
